I'll read both files completely before judging.Based on my complete review of both files, I checked every concrete claim against the findings and verified each citation key.

The section is overwhelmingly faithful and correctly cited. I found one faithfulness problem: in the salt-balance paragraph, the claim that salt removed exceeded salt added "cumulatively" is attributed to Manjunatha2004, but that source reports the opposite cumulatively (cumulative salts added ≈452.9 mg vs. removed ≈372.9 mg; removal exceeded input only in the first year: 125.4 vs. 119.8 mg).

{"passed": false, "unfaithful": ["\"salt removed exceeded salt added in the first year and cumulatively in well-functioning systems \\parencite{Manjunatha2004}\" -- the \"and cumulatively\" part is contradicted by Manjunatha2004, whose finding states cumulative salts added (about 452.9 mg) exceeded salts removed (about 372.9 mg); salt removal exceeded input only in the first year (125.4 vs 119.8 mg)."], "miscited": []}
